 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Victoria's unemployment rate is higher than NSW's.** In September 2026 (the latest month available, seasonally adjusted):\n\n- **Victoria: 5.1%** (5.05%)\n- **NSW: 4.7%** (4.71%)\n\nThe gap is about **0.34 percentage points**.\n\nThe gap has narrowed sharply in the past month. In August 2026, Victoria was at 5.17% and NSW at 4.35%, a gap of about 0.8 points. NSW rose by about 0.36 points in September, while Victoria eased slightly.",
